      "content": "Applying a hard countdown timer that remains unchanged for days is indeed risky, as it quickly erodes the brand's credibility and appears deceptive to savvy collectors. Since you discuss the Patek Philippe Nautilus, the industry standard suggests that maintaining a state of \"perpetual scarcity\" often works better than cycling through fake inventory numbers. Your best move is to keep the timer active only during actual restocks or sell-outs, ensuring the \"limited\" label always reflects genuine rather than manufactured urgency. This approach protects your reputation while still nudging the sales team toward true market-driven tactics instead of false anxieties.",
